{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"aa00000000000004","type":"group","x":-320,"y":680,"width":1120,"height":1230,"color":"4","label":"⚙️ Session 0 — System Services"},
		{"id":"aa0000000000000a","type":"group","x":950,"y":680,"width":990,"height":1230,"color":"5","label":"👤 Interactive User Session"},
		{"id":"aa00000000000001","type":"text","text":"# 🖥️ Windows Core Processes","x":750,"y":-520,"width":240,"height":120,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"aa00000000000002","type":"text","text":"## ⚙️ [[System]] — PID 4\nHosts kernel-mode threads. The root of all Windows processes.\n\n- **Image**: `ntoskrnl.exe`\n- **User**: NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM\n- **Parent**: None\n\n> Always PID 4. One instance. Starts at boot.","x":630,"y":-320,"width":550,"height":240,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"aa0000000000000c","type":"text","text":"## 🔑 [[winlogon.exe]] — Windows Logon\nControls the secure interactive logon experience.\n\n- **Path**: `C:\\Windows\\System32\\winlogon.exe`\n- **User**: NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM\n- **Parent**: smss.exe (exited)\n\n**Jobs**: Handles Ctrl+Alt+Del (SAS), coordinates logon with lsass.exe, loads user profile, launches userinit.exe, manages lock/unlock\n\n⚠️ **Key Registry (persistence risk)**\n`HKLM\\...\\Winlogon\\Shell` → `explorer.exe`\n`HKLM\\...\\Winlogon\\Userinit` → `userinit.exe,`\n\nUnexpected values here = active persistence mechanism","x":1420,"y":730,"width":480,"height":380,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"aa0000000000000d","type":"text","text":"## 👤 [[userinit.exe]] — User Init\nInitializes the user environment after logon, then exits.\n\n- **Path**: `C:\\Windows\\System32\\userinit.exe`\n- **User**: Logged-in user\n- **Parent**: winlogon.exe\n\n**Jobs**: Runs logon scripts, reconnects network drives, launches the shell (explorer.exe), then **exits**\n\n> Explorer's parent appears missing — this is normal and expected.","x":1420,"y":1180,"width":480,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"aa0000000000000e","type":"text","text":"## 🖥️ [[explorer.exe]] — Windows Shell\nThe graphical desktop environment for the user.\n\n- **Path**: `C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe`\n- **User**: Logged-in user (NOT SYSTEM)\n- **Parent**: userinit.exe (exited — normal)\n\n**Jobs**: Desktop, taskbar, Start menu, File Explorer, launches apps from user interaction\n\n⚠️ **Attack Vectors**\n- Masquerading: wrong path or misspelled name\n- Process injection (inherits user security context)\n- Suspicious outbound network connections\n\n**SOC**: Sysmon EID 1 (creation), EID 3 (network), EID 10 (injection attempt)","x":1420,"y":1470,"width":480,"height":360,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"aa00000000000006","type":"text","text":"## 🔧 [[wininit.exe]] — Windows Init\n*(Session 0)*\n\nInitializes essential system processes in Session 0.\n\n- **Path**: `C:\\Windows\\System32\\wininit.exe`\n- **User**: NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM\n- **Parent**: smss.exe (exited)\n- **Instances**: One\n\n**Starts**:\n- services.exe — Service Control Manager\n- lsass.exe — Security Authority\n- lsaiso.exe — (if Credential Guard enabled)","x":250,"y":836,"width":380,"height":283,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"aa00000000000008","type":"text","text":"## ⚙️ [[services.exe]] — Service Control Manager\nManages all Windows services and auto-start drivers.\n\n- **Path**: `C:\\Windows\\System32\\services.exe`\n- **User**: NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM\n- **Parent**: wininit.exe | **Instances**: One\n\n**Jobs**: Start/stop/monitor services, manage service DB, coordinate driver loading\n\n**Config**: `HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services`\n\n**SOC**: System EID 7045 (new service installed)","x":250,"y":1180,"width":380,"height":283,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"aa0000000000000b","type":"text","text":"## 🔵 [[csrss.exe]] — Win32 Subsystem\n*(Interactive Session)*\n\nSupports the Win32 subsystem for the user's session.\n\n- **Path**: `C:\\Windows\\System32\\csrss.exe`\n- **User**: NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM\n- **Session**: Interactive (≥ 1)\n- **Parent**: smss.exe (exited)\n\n> Separate instance from Session 0 csrss.\nParent exit is expected and normal.","x":990,"y":839,"width":380,"height":280,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"aa00000000000003","type":"text","text":"## 🗂️ [[smss.exe]] — Session Manager\nFirst user-mode process. Creates all Windows sessions.\n\n- **Path**: `C:\\Windows\\System32\\smss.exe`\n- **Parent**: System (PID 4)\n- **User**: NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM\n\n**Jobs**: Init sessions, start wininit + winlogon, set env variables, paging file setup\n\n> Master instance stays running. Session child instances exit after init.","x":600,"y":40,"width":580,"height":215,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"aa0000000000000f","type":"text","text":"## 📋 Two Ways a Service Can Run\n\n**A. DLL hosted by svchost.exe**\n```\nservices.exe\n  └── svchost.exe -k Group\n        └── service.dll\n             (no own PID)\n```\n- `ImagePath` → `svchost.exe -k <Group>`\n- `ServiceDll` → path to the .dll\n- Registry: `HKLM\\...\\Services\\<Name>\\Parameters`\n\n---\n\n**B. Standalone executable**\n```\nservices.exe\n  └── myservice.exe\n       (has its own PID)\n```\n- `ImagePath` → path directly to .exe\n\n---\n\n**How to identify**\n`sc.exe qc <ServiceName>`\n`tasklist /svc`\n`reg query HKLM\\...\\Services\\<Name>\\Parameters /v ServiceDll`\n\n⚠️ Malicious DLLs inside a legitimate svchost.exe make a trusted process execute malicious code. Always verify the ServiceDll path and signature.","x":1520,"y":-355,"width":560,"height":790,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"aa00000000000005","type":"text","text":"## 🔵 [[csrss.exe]] — Win32 Subsystem\n*(Session 0)*\n\nSupports the Win32 subsystem for the system session.\n\n- **Path**: `C:\\Windows\\System32\\csrss.exe`\n- **User**: NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM\n- **DLLs**: csrsrv.dll, basesrv.dll, winsrv.dll\n\n**Jobs**: Console mgmt, process/thread creation, shutdown handling\n\n> Parent (smss.exe) exits after init — this is normal.\nMultiple instances = one per active session.","x":-240,"y":836,"width":380,"height":283,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"aa00000000000007","type":"text","text":"## 🔐 [[lsass.exe]] — Local Security Authority\nWindows security checkpoint — handles all authentication.\n\n- **Path**: `C:\\Windows\\System32\\lsass.exe`\n- **User**: NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM\n- **Parent**: wininit.exe | **Instances**: One\n\n**Jobs**: Authenticates users (NTLM/Kerberos), creates access tokens, enforces security policy, generates audit events, handles password changes\n\n⚠️ **#1 Attack Target**\n- Credential dumping (Mimikatz, procdump)\n- Masquerading: fake lsass in wrong path\n- Protections: RunAsPPL, Credential Guard\n\n**SOC**: Sysmon EID 10 (Process Access to lsass)","x":-240,"y":1209,"width":380,"height":383,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"aa00000000000009","type":"text","text":"## 🔄 [[svchost.exe]] — Service Host\nHosts Windows services implemented as DLLs.\n\n- **Path**: `C:\\Windows\\System32\\svchost.exe`\n- **Parent**: services.exe\n- **User**: Varies (SYSTEM / LOCAL / NETWORK SERVICE)\n- **Command**: `svchost.exe -k <GroupName>`\n\n> Many instances are normal — each hosts one or more service DLLs.\n\n⚠️ Always verify:\n`HKLM\\...\\Services\\<Name>\\Parameters\\ServiceDll`\nNever trust the process name alone.","x":250,"y":1547,"width":380,"height":283,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"5e0f01ef5f067135","x":600,"y":2000,"width":580,"height":80,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"https://0xcybery.github.io/blog/Core-Processes-In-Windows-System"},
